From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc: dts: turris1x: rename the NAND partition

The NAND partition holds a UBI container whose rootfs volume carries the
root filesystem. With the partition itself called "rootfs",
CONFIG_MTD_ROOTFS_ROOT_DEV picks its mtdblock as the root device before
the ubiblock of the volume exists, and the kernel then looks for the
filesystem in the raw UBI container:

  ubi0: attached mtd7 (name "rootfs", size 256 MiB)
  block ubiblock0_1: created from ubi0:1(rootfs)
  No filesystem could mount root, tried: squashfs
  Kernel panic - not syncing: VFS: Unable to mount root fs on unknown-block(31,7)

Name the partition after what it is, a UBI container on the NAND, so that
the volume can be selected by name and the kernel command line does not
have to spell out a volume number.

"ubi" would do the same but has a second meaning: OpenWrt auto-attaches a
partition named "ubi" or "data" on any boot that passes no ubi.mtd=, using
the default VID header offset. This UBI is written with 2048, the offset
the factory bootloader expects, so such an attach only fails and logs an
error with a backtrace.

The microSD boot is exactly that case, and it must not attach the NAND:
mount_root would prefer a UBI rootfs_data over the one on the card, so a
card system would store its configuration in the NAND. Keeping the two
media apart should not rest on an attach that happens to fail, so the
partition is named outside the auto-attach set and every user of it names
it explicitly instead.

Signed-off-by: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
---
 arch/powerpc/boot/dts/turris1x.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/powerpc/boot/dts/turris1x.dts
+++ b/arch/powerpc/boot/dts/turris1x.dts
@@ -332,7 +332,7 @@
 				partition@0 {
 					/* 256 MB for UBI with one volume: UBIFS Root File System */
 					reg = <0x00000000 0x10000000>;
-					label = "rootfs";
+					label = "nand_ubi";
 				};
 			};
 		};
